# Wave W17-P (Route 116): echo post — a marker post at the tunnel mouth approach carrying two pale echo rings painted round its head, the rings the tunnel’s voice throws back (design: the bore was a Kin’s home first and a road second; its mouth is marked, not decorated). On echo turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s marker posts by the twin rings: this post marks a threshold you hear before you see.
